# CommonsBase_Build

## Overview

CMake, Ninja and VSWhere plus the Lua build rules (scriptmodules) that compile dk packages from source.

`CommonsBase_Build` is the build apparatus other dk packages use to compile
from source: the **CMake** and **Ninja** build tools, **VSWhere** for locating
MSVC on Windows, and the Lua **scriptmodules** (build rules) that drive them.

## Toolchain discovery

The `CommonsBase_Build.Toolchain.Discover.*` objects supply system-toolchain
discovery probes. A probe runs at execution time inside a consuming form
command, emits UTF-8 LF `KEY=VALUE` lines on stdout, and exits nonzero with
a one-line stderr message naming the per-ABI contract when the toolchain is
absent. Discovery data stays in process environment and configuration
files; it never enters dk values.

Provider contract (any dk package can ship an alternative provider):

+ The object slot tree contains `bin/discover.sh` and/or `bin/discover.bat`.
+ Invocation: `discover --abi <TARGET_ABI> [--config <path>]`.
+ Output keys match `[A-Z0-9_]+`.

Key registry:

| Provider | Keys |
|---|---|
| `Toolchain.Discover.MSVC` | `VSINSTALLDIR`, `VCToolsVersion`, `WindowsSDKVersion`, `VSCMD_VER`, `VisualStudioVersion`, `MSVS_PREFERENCE`, `DKML_COMPILE_VS_DIR`, `DKML_COMPILE_VS_VCVARSVER`, `DKML_COMPILE_VS_WINSDKVER`, `DKML_COMPILE_VS_MSVSPREFERENCE`, `DKML_COMPILE_VS_CMAKEGENERATOR` |
| `Toolchain.Discover.CGlibc` | `DK_TC_CC`, `DK_TC_CXX`, `DK_TC_AS`, `DK_TC_AR`, `DK_TC_LD`, `DK_TC_GLIBC_VERSION` |

Configuration files (`toolchains.jsonc`), highest precedence first:

1. The project-level `etc/dk/t/toolchains.jsonc` (git-ignored; it names
   paths on one machine).
2. The user/machine-level `<xdg config>/dk/toolchains.jsonc`
   (`$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/dk`, default `~/.config/dk`, on Unix;
   `%LOCALAPPDATA%\dk` on Windows).
3. The host probe.

Schema: a `toolchains` object keyed by target ABI name or family glob
(`Windows_*`, `Linux_*`, `Linux_*_musl`, `Darwin_*`). Keys per section:
`provider` (module@version of the Discover object), `msvs_preference`
(ordered `;`-separated glob list over `VS<major>.<minor>` identifiers,
the existing `MSVS_PREFERENCE` syntax), `vs_dir`, `cc`, `cxx`, `as`,
`ar`, `ld`, `binutils_prefix`. A value is a literal path, or a dk value
expression beginning with `$(` that `dk0 dialog
CommonsBase_Build.Toolchain.Discover.<Family>` resolves under the `run`
and `write` trust caps into the `resolved` section (with a `fingerprint`
staleness token). Hand-written keys override the `resolved` cache.

